#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087531 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5fb4d6b-2c86-5ad6-898b-5a1cd44e4106" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing and Solving a Characteristic Equation With Repeated Roots"}] :question/id #uuid "81531c55-fe2e-5eff-82ba-9e08abf24a0e" :question/math-academy-id "e-6591" :question/problem "Consider the equation $y''-2y'+y = 0$. If $y = e^{\\lambda x}$ is a solution to the equation, then what is $\\lambda$?" :question/worked-solution "Assuming\n\n$$\ny=e^{\\lambda x}\n$$\n\nand differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\ny'= \\lambda e^{\\lambda x},\\qquad y''= \\lambda^2 e^{\\lambda x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ^{2}e^{λx} - 2λe^{λx} + e^{λx} &= 0 \\\\\ne^{λx}(λ^{2} - 2λ + 1) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ^{2} - 2λ + 1 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(λ - 1)^{2} &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda = 1$ is a repeated root of the auxiliary equation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087532 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bebe4460-e57e-546f-99c8-81192aafc1ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions When the Characteristic Equation Has Repeated Roots"}] :question/id #uuid "3363cf38-10a2-5a55-9451-ee2101b8e809" :question/math-academy-id "e-6592" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n$\\frac{\\textrm{d}^2 y}{\\textrm{d} t^2} - 12\\frac{\\textrm{d} y}{\\textrm{d} t} + 36y =0$." :question/worked-solution "Assuming\n\n$$\ny=e^{\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nand differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d} y}{\\textrm{d} t}= \\lambda e^{\\lambda t},\\qquad \\frac{\\textrm{d}^2 y}{\\textrm{d} t^2}= \\lambda^2 e^{\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ^{2}e^{λt} - 12λe^{λt} + 36e^{λt} &= 0 \\\\\ne^{λt}(λ^{2} - 12λ + 36) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ^{2} - 12λ + 36 &= 0 \\\\\n(λ - 6)^{2} &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda = 6$ is a repeated root. Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny = Ae^{6 t} + Bte^{6t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087533 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ad20bb-c6a4-5390-a11a-e5277cfd1667" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Non-Solutions of Second-Order Homogeneous ODEs"}] :question/id #uuid "abc842b6-8b86-585c-a425-5776909c6425" :question/math-academy-id "e-6593" :question/problem "Given the equation $y''+12y'+36y = 0$ for $y=y(x)$, which of the following is **not** a solution to this equation?\n\n1. $xe^{-6x}$\n2. $4e^{-6x}-3xe^{-6x}$\n3. $2e^{6x}$" :question/worked-solution "Assuming\n\n$$\ny=e^{\\lambda x}\n$$\n\nand differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\ny'= \\lambda e^{\\lambda x},\\qquad y''= \\lambda^2 e^{\\lambda x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ^{2}e^{λx} + 12λe^{λx} + 36e^{λx} &= 0 \\\\\ne^{λx}(λ^{2} + 12λ + 36) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ^{2} + 12λ + 36 &= 0 \\\\\n(λ + 6)^{2} &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda =-6$ is a repeated root. Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny = Ae^{-6 x} + Bxe^{-6x}\n$$\n\nFinally, we need to determine whether each of the given functions takes the form shown above.\n\n- Function I takes the above form with $A=0$ and $B=1$. So, it is a solution to the given ODE.\n- Function II takes the above form with $A=4$ and $B=-3$. So, it is a solution to the given ODE.\n- Function III does *not* take the above form. It contains $e^{6x}$, which is not included in the above form. So, it is *not* a solution to the given ODE.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ad20bb-c6a4-5390-a11a-e5277cfd1667" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Non-Solutions of Second-Order Homogeneous ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5d6c996-6880-5155-8e02-91204a257bdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{7t} - 4te^{7t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086018} {:answer/id #uuid "dafe28d5-e4e6-516c-aee9-29227e9392db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14e^{7t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086019} {:answer/id #uuid "e0d1d3fc-e6d3-5217-a0f6-694b077b8d80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{7t} - 2te^{7t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086020} {:answer/id #uuid "307ad8f7-c6b6-555e-bfa0-b136a5a7745c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2te^{7t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086021} {:answer/id #uuid "65ec4f8e-b72d-55c1-b920-606a32a5ee8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7e^{t} + te^{7t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65ec4f8e-b72d-55c1-b920-606a32a5ee8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7e^{t} + te^{7t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086022} :answer-field/id #uuid "592c9c68-4d8c-509f-bb6b-2f2a364a5e53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086017}] :question/id #uuid "41fb4ba9-2a2a-520b-a6ad-5cdc344e0ff5" :question/math-academy-id "q-64798" :question/problem "Given the equation $y^{″} - 14y^{′} + 49y = 0$ for $y = y(t)$, which of the following is **not** a solution to this equation?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088291 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bebe4460-e57e-546f-99c8-81192aafc1ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions When the Characteristic Equation Has Repeated Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8117739d-fe67-5c18-8b00-605ec83cb2c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = Ae^{x/2} + Bxe^{x/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086677} {:answer/id #uuid "9f74c7cd-4e00-5a82-8956-dee7dcb99875" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = Ae^{3x/2} + Bxe^{3x/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086678} {:answer/id #uuid "b461765b-ba55-5ebf-8da3-f2df24c16e4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = Ae^{3x} + Be^{x/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086679} {:answer/id #uuid "e14d30fc-6522-5f8f-91f6-ea02c8846549" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = Ae^{3x/2} + Bxe^{-3x/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086680} {:answer/id #uuid "ebff4e66-3e32-5ba0-965a-332a76cb75dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = Ae^{3x/2} + Be^{-x/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f74c7cd-4e00-5a82-8956-dee7dcb99875" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = Ae^{3x/2} + Bxe^{3x/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086678} :answer-field/id #uuid "5db49140-2925-583b-b643-9a53f11c318f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086676}] :question/id #uuid "8baa66ad-4610-5025-9c74-4f7852b717ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-7795" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} - 3\\frac{dy}{dx} + \\frac{9}{4}y = 0$."}]}
